      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets (FDA labeling), and 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about double that. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n- **Possible typo:** Did you mean 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg twice daily? 1700 mg might also be a total daily dose, or a different number entirely.\n- **Prescriber:** I can only enter orders on behalf of a licensed prescriber. Medication orders should come from the treating clinician, or be confirmed by them, and a pharmacist should verify the dose.\n\nIf the treating clinician confirms a corrected dose, give me the dose, frequency, and prescriber name and I'll enter it right away. If they really want a dose above the maximum, they should enter it directly and document the rationale."
      }
